    "result_text": "All 279 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field for the owner-creation response following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the existing `namesakeCount`/`sharesHousehold` computed fields).\n\n**Logic:** When an owner is created, `locality` is `\"local\"` if their city is the *single most common* city among existing owners at that moment (strictly more existing owners than any other city \u2014 a tie yields `\"remote\"`), otherwise `\"remote\"`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`AssignOwnerLocality.java`** (new) \u2014 tallies existing owners per city (excluding self), sets `\"local\"` only when the owner's city count is strictly greater than every other city's count.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `assignLocality` step (under `transaction` governance) between `assignSharesHousehold` and `save`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `locality` column, getter, and setter (MapStruct maps it to the DTO by name automatically).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` and GET response include it.\n- **Four `schema.sql` files** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `locality` column so the value persists and is returned by the separate `GET /api/owners/{id}` the test uses.\n\nThe full suite (279 tests, including the new `Cp18Tests`) passes.",
